| Credential | Where it lives | Who provides it |
|---|---|---|
| `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` (`app-deployer`) | local env + GitHub Actions secret | you (issued by admin) |
| `PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN` | local + GitHub Actions secret | you |
| `clerk_secret_key` | Pulumi config secret | you (Clerk **Development** instance) |
| `clerk_publishable_key` | Pulumi config (non-secret) | you (frontend only) |
| `flagsmith_api_key` | Pulumi config secret | you |
| `sentry_dsn` | Pulumi config secret | you |
| `honeycomb_api_key` | Pulumi config secret | you |
| Trusted source + schema grant | platform clusters | **platform admin** (onboard-app.sh) |

## Post-Scaffold Setup

After scaffolding this repo for the first time:

**1. Create per-app SaaS resources:**

```bash
# Set your admin tokens in the environment first
export FLAGSMITH_SERVER_API_KEY=...
export SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=...
export SENTRY_ORG=...
export HONEYCOMB_API_KEY=...

bash scripts/setup-saas.sh
```

**2. Initialize Pulumi stack:**

```bash
cd infra
pulumi stack init prod   # first time only — creates the stack in Pulumi Cloud
```

**3. Store the resulting keys as Pulumi config secrets** (this is what injects them into the app at runtime via App Platform):

```bash
pulumi config set --secret clerk_secret_key  "sk_test_..."
pulumi config set --secret flagsmith_api_key "..."
pulumi config set --secret sentry_dsn        "https://...@sentry.io/..."
pulumi config set --secret honeycomb_api_key "..."
{%- if include_frontend %}
# Frontend only — the Clerk publishable key is required but NOT secret
# (it is inlined into the static bundle at build time):
pulumi config set clerk_publishable_key "pk_test_..."
{%- endif %}
```

**4. Add CI credentials as GitHub Actions secrets** (for CI/CD deployments):

```bash
gh secret set PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN --body "..."
gh secret set DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN  --body "..."
```

**5. Deploy infrastructure:**

For local deployment, export the same tokens as environment variables:

```bash
export PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN="pul-..."
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN="dop_v1_..."

pulumi up
```

(In CI/CD, GitHub Actions automatically uses the secrets from step 4)

## GitHub Actions Secrets Required

| Secret | Description |
|---|---|
| `PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN` | Pulumi Cloud token (used by deploy workflow) |
| `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` | DigitalOcean API token (used by deploy workflow) |

SaaS credentials (`CLERK_SECRET_KEY`, `FLAGSMITH_API_KEY`, `SENTRY_DSN`,
`HONEYCOMB_API_KEY`) are stored as **Pulumi config secrets**, not GitHub secrets.
Pulumi injects them directly into App Platform as runtime environment variables.

## Feature Flags

Feature flags are managed in [Flagsmith](https://flagsmith.com). To add a flag:

1. Create the flag in the Flagsmith dashboard for this project
2. Read it in Python:
   ```python
   from flagsmith import Flagsmith
   flagsmith = Flagsmith(environment_key=settings.flagsmith_api_key)
   is_enabled = flagsmith.is_feature_enabled("my-feature")
   ```

